package com.bqsqwad.heartbreakhealer.feature.entertainment

internal object StoryLibraryBatch2 {
    val stories = listOf(
        StorySeries("the_midnight_archive","The Midnight Archive","A student volunteer discovers that a town's forgotten records can change its future.", listOf(
            StoryPart(1,"The Locked Room",listOf("On her first evening volunteering at the town archive, Kemi noticed a door behind the map cabinet. It had no handle, only a brass plate engraved with a crescent moon.","The archivist said the room had been sealed after a flood. Yet a thin line of warm light showed beneath it, and a fresh card on Kemi's desk read: 'Start with the year the river changed course.'")),
            StoryPart(2,"The River Year",listOf("Old newspapers recorded a flood in 1978 that changed the river's path. The archive catalogue listed three missing boxes from that year, all marked as transferred.","Kemi found the transfer signature belonged to a librarian named Mr Adeyemi. His granddaughter now lived nearby and agreed to speak with her.")),
            StoryPart(3,"A Granddaughter's Memory",listOf("The granddaughter remembered her grandfather describing a collection of letters from families displaced by the flood. He believed the letters could help settle a boundary dispute, but officials had dismissed them as unreliable.","She gave Kemi a notebook with a sketch of the archive basement and a note: 'The moon marks the dry shelf.'")),
            StoryPart(4,"The Dry Shelf",listOf("Kemi and the archivist inspected the basement after receiving permission. Behind a row of damaged atlases stood a shelf untouched by the flood.","A metal box held the missing letters, each carefully dated and signed. One envelope contained a surveyor's map that showed the river before and after the flood.")),
            StoryPart(5,"The Mapmaker",listOf("The map bore the signature of a surveyor whose work had been questioned because the official copy was incomplete. Kemi located his field journal in a university collection.","The journal confirmed that the map was accurate. It also explained that the surveyor had left a duplicate with the archive because he feared the original would be altered.")),
            StoryPart(6,"The Second Copy",listOf("A note in the journal named the archive's former caretaker as the person who received the duplicate. The caretaker's son found a sealed tube among family keepsakes.","Inside was a second map and a receipt showing that the town council had accepted it. The dispute had continued because the receipt was filed under the wrong district name.")),
            StoryPart(7,"The Council Record",listOf("Kemi presented the documents to the archive board. They verified the paper, signatures, and dates, then arranged a public review with the council's land office.","The official admitted the records had been overlooked, not destroyed. A new survey would compare the historical map with present-day measurements.")),
            StoryPart(8,"The Public Review",listOf("Residents from both sides of the river attended. The letters revealed where old footpaths, gardens, and shared wells had stood before the flood.","Rather than argue over rumours, the families agreed to let the verified survey guide the boundary decision. Kemi noticed the granddaughter quietly holding her grandfather's notebook.")),
            StoryPart(9,"A Fair Boundary",listOf("The survey confirmed the historic route and corrected the public map. The council established a shared access path and recognised the families whose records had preserved the evidence.","The archive board voted to digitise the flood collection so it could never be misplaced so easily again. The locked room was opened as a small local-history gallery.")),
            StoryPart(10,"What the Records Remember",listOf("At the gallery opening, Kemi placed the surveyor's journal beside the two maps. The archivist thanked her for treating every letter as a person's memory rather than an inconvenient old paper.","The granddaughter donated her grandfather's notebook, and the council published the corrected boundary record. The mystery ended without a villainous secret: it had been a chain of filing mistakes, silence, and forgotten names. Kemi turned the crescent key over in her palm and understood the archive's lesson—history becomes useful when people are willing to check it, share it, and correct it."))
        )),
        StorySeries("the_green_rooftop","The Green Rooftop","A school garden project uncovers a generous plan hidden above the city.", listOf(
            StoryPart(1,"A Patch of Green",listOf("When Feyi's class was assigned the unused rooftop, most students imagined a dusty place for old chairs. Feyi saw a chance to build a garden where the neighbourhood could learn to grow food.","Under a loose tile she found a small tin labelled 'For the next gardeners'. Inside was a seed list and a drawing of the roof from twenty years earlier.")),
            StoryPart(2,"The Old Drawing",listOf("The drawing showed raised beds, rain barrels, and a shaded reading corner. A name at the bottom—Mrs Nwosu—matched the retired science teacher who lived two streets away.","Mrs Nwosu said the garden had been planned but never completed after the school roof needed repairs. She still had the original permission letter.")),
            StoryPart(3,"Permission First",listOf("The principal agreed to inspect the roof with a qualified maintenance team before any work began. The students learned that a good project needed safety checks, a budget, and a clear plan.","The inspection confirmed that one section could support lightweight planters. The team marked off the restricted areas and redesigned the garden around the safe zone.")),
            StoryPart(4,"The Seed List",listOf("The tin's seed list included herbs and vegetables suited to containers. Mrs Nwosu explained that the list had been made with a local gardening group.","Feyi found a note beside the list: 'Ask the market women what grows well here.' The students visited the market and collected practical advice from experienced growers.")),
            StoryPart(5,"A Missing Sponsor",listOf("The permission letter mentioned a sponsor who had promised soil and tools, but the sponsor's name was smudged. The school secretary found an old invoice with a logo from a nursery that had since changed owners.","The new owner recognised the project and offered to check the company's archived records before making any promise.")),
            StoryPart(6,"The Nursery Ledger",listOf("The ledger showed that the original donation had been paid for, but delivery was cancelled when the roof repairs began. The credit remained on the account for years.","The nursery offered the school the equivalent supplies, and the students wrote a public thank-you rather than treating the discovery as an entitlement.")),
            StoryPart(7,"The First Planters",listOf("With the roof cleared and approved, the students assembled lightweight containers and added suitable growing mix. They labelled each plant and created a watering rota.","A week later, several seedlings looked weak. Instead of guessing, the class asked the market growers to help them review sunlight, drainage, and watering.")),
            StoryPart(8,"Learning to Adjust",listOf("The students moved the sun-loving plants and changed the watering schedule. The garden improved, and the class recorded what worked so next year's students could learn from it.","Mrs Nwosu brought a photograph of the rooftop as it had once been imagined. The new garden was smaller, but its paths and reading corner made it welcoming.")),
            StoryPart(9,"The Open Day",listOf("Families visited the rooftop on a Saturday. Students explained how they had checked the structure, planned the budget, and learned from early mistakes.","The market growers donated a few more seedlings, while the nursery helped install a simple rainwater collection system approved by the school.")),
            StoryPart(10,"Seeds for Tomorrow",listOf("The principal announced that the rooftop would remain a student-led learning garden, with clear safety rules and a yearly handover team. Feyi placed the original seed list in a display case beside the new garden plan.","The tin had not contained treasure or a secret fortune. It had contained something more useful: a project waiting for the right people to finish it. As the class harvested its first herbs, Feyi wrote a new label for the tin—'For the next gardeners, too'—and left it ready for the students who would follow."))
        )),
        StorySeries("the_blue_notebook","The Blue Notebook","A missing notebook helps three friends uncover the truth behind a celebrated school song.", listOf(
            StoryPart(1,"The Empty Music Stand",listOf("The school choir was preparing for its anniversary when the music teacher discovered that the original blue notebook was missing. It held the earliest draft of the school song.","A rumour blamed a former student who had left after a disagreement. Amara, the choir's new pianist, decided to look for evidence before repeating the story.")),
            StoryPart(2,"A Different Melody",listOf("The printed song credited one composer, but a recording in the media room included a second voice suggesting changes to the melody.","Amara asked the retired music teacher, who remembered that two students had written the song together. Their names were Tunde and Bisi.")),
            StoryPart(3,"The Recording",listOf("The recording was stored on an old cassette. The school technician helped transfer it carefully, and the choir heard both students discussing lyrics and rhythm.","At the end, Bisi said she would keep the notebook until the final version was approved. The trail led to a community arts centre.")),
            StoryPart(4,"The Arts Centre",listOf("The centre's director remembered Bisi, now a music tutor. Bisi was surprised that the school still used the song but said she had never been asked about its history.","She explained that she had returned the notebook years ago, placing it in the music department's cabinet after the anniversary committee postponed the celebration.")),
            StoryPart(5,"The Cabinet Key",listOf("The old cabinet had been replaced, and its contents moved into storage. The inventory listed a blue notebook, but the box number was missing.","A caretaker remembered moving a box marked 'choir' to the stage loft. The students asked the school manager to supervise the search.")),
            StoryPart(6,"Under the Stage",listOf("They found the box beneath spare stage curtains. The notebook was inside, along with drafts in two different handwritings and a letter from the former headteacher.","The letter explained that the committee had printed the song credit incorrectly and planned to correct it at the next anniversary. The correction was never made after the event was postponed.")),
            StoryPart(7,"Finding Tunde",listOf("The school contacted Tunde, who now worked as a sound engineer. He confirmed that he and Bisi had composed the song together and said he had always hoped the record would be corrected.","He did not want a public argument. He simply wanted both names included and the students to understand how collaboration works.")),
            StoryPart(8,"A New Arrangement",listOf("Amara invited both composers to hear the choir's new arrangement. Bisi suggested a softer introduction, while Tunde improved the harmony for the final verse.","The students added a short spoken introduction explaining the song's history and the two creators' contributions.")),
            StoryPart(9,"The Anniversary",listOf("At the anniversary concert, the headteacher announced the corrected credit. Tunde and Bisi stood together as the choir performed the song, and the audience gave them a warm welcome.","The blue notebook was placed in the school archive with a digital copy available to students. The rumour about the former student's departure was formally corrected.")),
            StoryPart(10,"Both Names",listOf("After the concert, Bisi told Amara that the best part was hearing a new generation sing the melody without carrying the old misunderstanding. Tunde promised to visit the choir's next rehearsal.","Amara wrote both composers' names on the music stand card. The notebook had been found, the credit had been restored, and the school song finally told the truth about the people who made it."))
        ))
    )
}
